From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanislav Gabenov <gabenovstan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: octeon: keep legacy PCI IRQ mapper after init

octeon_pci_pcibios_map_irq() is assigned to the global
octeon_pcibios_map_irq pointer.  PCI drivers may call it after init memory
has been released when they are loaded as modules.

Drop __init to avoid calling freed code.  This fixes a reserved instruction
exception when ath9k probes on the D-Link DAP-2690 A1.

Signed-off-by: Stanislav Gabenov <gabenovstan@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/mips/pci/pci-octeon.c
+++ b/arch/mips/pci/pci-octeon.c
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@ const char *octeon_get_pci_interrupts(vo
  * @pin:    The PCI interrupt pin read from the device, then swizzled
  * Returns Interrupt number for the device
  */
-int __init octeon_pci_pcibios_map_irq(const struct pci_dev *dev,
+int octeon_pci_pcibios_map_irq(const struct pci_dev *dev,
 				      u8 slot, u8 pin)
 {
 	int irq_num;
